Praise.; Applausibilitas. @SE 2993.

Praise.; Laus.
Praise.; Laudare.

@AC 456. To praise and celebrate the Lord is not an active life; but the effect of that life; for the Lord has no need of praises; but wills us to perform the goods of charity... @HH 404. @SE 3986.

@1171[3]. These are "the praises of Jehovah" (Isaiah 60:6); that is, internal worship.

@1483. "They praised her to Pharaoh" (Genesis 12:15) = that they were pleasing.

@3048[5]. Goods and truths, which are "the praises of Jehovah." 3242[2].

@3796[3]. Attends only to the delight... from the praise... of self.

@3880[5]. "Enter... His courts in praise" (Psalms 100:4)... "Praise" is from the love of truth.

@5236[4]. "From the mouth of infants... Thou hast perfected praise" (Matthew 21:16) = that praise can come to the Lord through noway except through innocence...

@8303. To be "venerated with praises" (Exodus 15:11) = that to Him alone are the glory and thanksgiving. Explained.

@8337[4]. To "praise with the timbrel" (Psalms 149:3) = to glorify from the delight of the affection of the good of faith; and to "praise with the harp" = from the pleasantness of the affection of the truth of faith.

@HH 553. When others praise, venerate, and worship them, their faces are contracted, and appear as if glad...

@556[end]. Among those he calls his own are all who praise... him. @NJHD 67.

@AR 809. "Praise our God" (Revelation 19:5) = (an influx that) they should worship! the Lord as the only God of Heaven.

@--[2]. That to "praise God" = to worship Him; and thence that His praise is His worship. Illustrated.

@CL 16. They whispered a votive praise to the Lord, and (then) reposed themselves at the table.

@SE 2993. While writing he continually reflects on self-praise.

@DMin 4676[end]. He could praise no one from his heart.

@AE 324[9]. To "announce the praises of Jehovah" = evangelization concerning the Lord, and the worship of Him.

@376[12]. Worship from these things is signified by to "praise Jehovah..." (Isaiah 62:9).

@--[23]. To "praise the gods of gold..." = worship from the love of self...

@388[25]. To "praise Jehovah" (Psalms 148) = to worship Him. @401[23]. @419[15].

@455[15]. "Praise" is predicated of the truth of the doctrine of the Church.

@504[25]. To "praise" = to worship. @587[17]. @630[13].

@730[29]. Their joy from the preaching and Knowledge of truth, is meant by to "sing praise and lift up the voice" (Isaiah 42:10).

@1210. "Praise God all His servants" (Revelation 19:5) = the worship of the Lord by those in truths. To "praise God" = to confess and worship Him. Illustrated.

Praise, To sing.; Psallere.

@AC 3880[4]. To "sing praise" (Psalms 57:9) relates to what is spiritual. @AE 323[6].

@8633[end]. (The inhabitants of Jupiter) sing praise (at sunrise and sunset).

@AE 323[7]. Confession... from spiritual truth is expressed by "sing praise on the harp to God" (Psalms 147:7).

@326[11]. Joy therefrom is described by To "sing praise," etc.

