@2219[5]. The love of self is not always that which appears in the external form as haughtiness -fastus-, and pride; for sometimes these can have charity towards the neighbour; for such an external is born with some, and by some is contracted in early life; but is afterwards subjugated; the external still remaining.

@2220[2]. "Pride" (Zephaniah 2:10) = the love of self.

@--[3]. "Pride" (Ezekiel 16:49) = the love of self.

