@9820[2]. The prophets are called "holy" because by them is signified the Word, which is the Divine truth; and, in special, doctrines from the Word.

@9954[9]. The reason the prophets were anointed, was that the prophets represented the Lord as to the doctrine of Divine truth, consequently as to the Word. @AE 375[15].

@10683[6]. "A disciple" = the truth of life; "a prophet," the truth of doctrine.

