@801. "In her was found the blood of prophets and of saints" (Revelation 18:24) = the adulteration and profanation of every truth of the Word and of the Church... "Prophets" = all who are in Divine truths from the Word; and, abstractedly, the truths of doctrine from the Word.

@819. "The testimony of Jesus is the spirit of prophecy" (Revelation 19:10) = that it is the all of the Word and of the doctrine thence.

@943. "The Lord God of the holy prophets" (Revelation 22:6) = the Lord from whom is the Word of both Covenants; for by "prophets" are signified those who teach truths from the Word; and, in the abstract sense, the doctrine of truth of the Church; and, in a wide sense, the Word itself, (thus) the Word of both Covenants.

@944. "Blessed is he that keepeth the words of this prophecy" (Revelation 22:7) = that the Lord will give eternal life to those who keep and do the truths or precepts of the doctrine of this Book, now opened by the Lord.

@946. "I am... of thy brethren the prophets" (Revelation 22:9) = those who are in the doctrine of the New Jerusalem.

@947. "Seal not the words of this prophecy" (Revelation 22:10) = that the Apocalypse is not to be closed up.

@957. "Everyone that heareth the words of the prophecy of this Book" (Revelation 22:18) = those who read and know the truths of doctrine of this Book now opened by the Lord. @958.

